-- title:
--   Pairwise commutation of Hecke and diamond operators on H¹
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \in \mathbb{N}$, a commutative ring $\kappa$, and a $\kappa$-linear representation $X$ of the group $\Gamma_{\bot}(N) :=$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH N ⊥`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ whose associated unit `gamma0Units N γ` of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ is trivial. Let $M$ be a submonoid of the multiplicative monoid of integral $2\times 2$ matrices such that the underlying matrix of every $g \in \Gamma_0(N)$ lies in $M$, and let $\rho' : M \to \mathrm{End}_\kappa(X)$ be a monoid homomorphism with $X.\rho(\gamma) = \rho'$ of the underlying matrix of $\gamma$, for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_{\bot}(N)$. Let $\iota$ be a type and $T : \iota \to \mathrm{End}_\kappa(H^1(\Gamma_{\bot}(N), X))$ a family of $\kappa$-linear endomorphisms of `groupCohomology.H1 X` such that for each $i$ one of the following holds: (1) there are a prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1) \in M$ and a proof $h\varphi$ that $\varphi := \rho'(\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1))$ satisfies `IsTwist` for the homomorphism `cTop N ⊥ ℓ` from `GammaHUpper N ⊥ ℓ` (the elements of $\Gamma_{\bot}(N)$ whose upper right entry vanishes mod $\ell$) to the top subgroup of $\Gamma_{\bot}(N)$, namely $\varphi(X.\rho(c\,s)\,a) = X.\rho(s)(\varphi\,a)$ for all such $s$ and all $a$, and $T i =$ `heckeH1` of these data, the endomorphism of $H^1$ induced by the corresponding twisted transfer operator on $1$-cocycles; or (2) there are $\sigma \in \Gamma_0(N)$ and a proof that $\rho'$ of the underlying matrix of $\sigma^{-1}$ is a twist for the endomorphism $\gamma \mapsto \sigma\gamma\sigma^{-1}$ of $\Gamma_{\bot}(N)$ (given by `conjHom N ⊥ σ`, viewed between top subgroups), with $T i$ the associated `heckeH1` operator. The conclusion is that $T i$ and $T j$ commute for all $i, j \in \iota$.
--
--   This is the commutativity of the algebra generated by the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ for $\ell \nmid N$ together with the diamond operators, realised here on $H^1$ of the level-$N$ group with coefficients in a representation whose action extends to a monoid of integral matrices. It is the input that allows simultaneous eigenvectors to be treated, and is used in the analysis of eigensystems on $H^1$ leading to the dichotomy between Eisenstein behaviour and the expected Hecke relations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HeckeCohomology_commute_of_forall_eq_heckeH1_cTop_or_eq_heckeH1_conjHom_of_forall_rep_eq_monoidHom_submonoid.lean

